+// Alpha mask coverage of the pixel. Multisampled (alpha to coverage), the mask's edge becomes the
+// fraction of samples it covers, sharpened to about a pixel: a needle thinner than a pixel covers
+// part of it instead of flipping on and off as the view moves. Otherwise kept or not at the cutoff.
+float maskCoverage(float alpha, float cutoff) {
+  if (!alphaToCoverage)
+    return alpha < cutoff ? 0.0 : 1.0;
+  return clamp((alpha - cutoff) / max(fwidth(alpha), 0.0001) + 0.5, 0.0, 1.0);
+}
